</article-title><source>Pfl&#x000fc;gers Arch.</source><volume>418</volume><year>1991</year><fpage>523</fpage><lpage>530</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="Malmqvistetal1999"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Malmqvist</surname><given-names>U.</given-names></name><name><surname>L&#x000f6;fgren</surname><given-names>M.</given-names></name><name><surname>Arner</surname><given-names>A.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Effects of ATP, ADP and inorganic phosphate on force and shortening velocity differ between fast and slow smooth muscles</article-title><source>Biophys. J.</source><volume>76</volume><year>1999</year><fpage>A284</fpage><lpage>A284</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="Mannherz1968"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Mannherz</surname><given-names>H.G.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>ATP-cleavage and ATP-diffusion in oscillating muscle fibers</article-title><source>Pfl&#x000fc;gers Arch.</source><volume>303</volume><year>1968</year><fpage>230</fpage><lpage>248</lpage></citation></ref><ref id="MarstonandTaylor1980"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Marston</surname><given-names>S.B.</given-names></name><name><surname>Taylor</surname><given-names>E.W.</given-names></name></person-group><article-title>Comparison of the myosin and actomyosin ATPase mechanisms of the four types of vertebrate muscles</article-title><source>J. Mol. Biol.</source><volume>139</volume><year>1980</year><fpage>573</fpage><lpage>600</lpage><pub-id pub-id-type="pmid">6447797</pub-id></citation></ref><ref id="Matthewetal1998"><citation citation-type="journal"><person-group person-group-type="author"><name><surname>Matthew</surname><given-names>J.D.</given-names></name><name><surname>Khromov</surname><given-names>A.S.</given-names></name><name><surname>Trybus</surname><given-names>K.M.</given-name